BT 0.75 0.60 1 rg /F1 9 Tf 62 273.5 Td (Question 2: 'How did you handle file uploads and PDF downloads with Axios?') Tj ET
BT 0.85 0.90 0.95 rg /F2 8.5 Tf 62 259.5 Td (Answer: 'For file uploads like PDF compression and multi-image conversion, I assembled multipart/form-data) Tj ET
BT 0.85 0.90 0.95 rg /F2 8.5 Tf 62 246.5 Td (payloads and created a request interceptor to strip default application/json headers, allowing the browser to) Tj ET
BT 0.85 0.90 0.95 rg /F2 8.5 Tf 62 233.5 Td (set the correct boundary. For downloads, Spring Boot streams ResponseEntity<byte[]> as application/pdf.) Tj ET
BT 0.85 0.90 0.95 rg /F2 8.5 Tf 62 220.5 Td (Standard Axios interceptors strip non-JSON bodies, so I enhanced our response interceptor to detect Blob) Tj ET
BT 0.85 0.90 0.95 rg /F2 8.5 Tf 62 207.5 Td (instances, verify whether an error JSON was encapsulated inside the blob, and pipe the binary stream directly) Tj ET
BT 0.85 0.90 0.95 rg /F2 8.5 Tf 62 194.5 Td (to an in-memory Object URL \(window.URL.createObjectURL\) to trigger instantaneous client-side file downloads) Tj ET
BT 0.85 0.90 0.95 rg /F2 8.5 Tf 62 181.5 Td (with zero data loss.') Tj ET
